# THE DATA LEMMA, DATE-TIME HALF, OUT OF PROFILE (SPEC.md §5.2; issue #135): the
# datetime-asserted.ttl shape with one :created assertion changed to a day that
# does not exist, 2023-02-30 (February has 28 days in 2023). That literal is not
# a valid dateTimeStamp, so :created is NOT literal-asserted: its range and all
# of its assertions stay out of profile as omissions. :issued is still valid
# and inert. The verdict is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2). The disjointness and the
# typing of :j are still read.

@prefix :     <https://example.org/> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:C rdfs:subClassOf :A .
:A owl:disjointWith :B .

:created a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "The date and time at which the element was created." ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTimeStamp .
:issued a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .

:j a :C ; :created "2024-11-22T03:00:01Z"^^xsd:dateTimeStamp .
:k a :B ; :created "2023-02-30T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTimeStamp .
:l a :D ; :created "2024-11-22T03:00:01Z"^^xsd:dateTimeStamp .

:j :issued "2024-02-29T24:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
:k :issued "2024-02-29T12:00:00+05:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
